#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""clawbook - manage the clawbook-lehre container from the inside.

Without arguments an interactive menu starts. Every subcommand accepts
--json: then stdout carries nothing but JSON (for the Windows script) and
the exit code tells success (0) or failure (non-zero).

    clawbook                        interactive menu
    clawbook status [--json]        interface version, build, services, home,
                                    package cache, restore after a new image
    clawbook check [--quiet|--json] are all tools of the image present?
    clawbook key show [--private]   public key and fingerprint (or private key)
    clawbook key new [--yes]        new key pair, replaces the old one
    clawbook stand [--write]        derived state (courses, packages, VS Code)
    clawbook kurse [--json]         installed courses
    clawbook kurs vscode <id>       merged course description for VS Code
    clawbook github status [--json] is gh logged in to GitHub? (never prompts)
    clawbook github login           GitHub login with gh (needs a terminal)
    clawbook github identitaet      git user.name/user.email from the GitHub
                                    account (asks; --json only reports)
    clawbook notebooklm [--yes]     NotebookLM login state; offers the cookie
                                    fix when the login is incomplete
    clawbook wsm status|erneuern    detect an outdated wsm configuration
                                    (single location ~/source) and renew it
    clawbook pakete katalog         technology and course packages (clawbook-apt)
    clawbook pakete add|remove <name...> [--yes] [--vorladen]
    clawbook pakete vorladen        PlatformIO platform for ESP32 (pioarduino)
    clawbook wiederherstellen       install packages from stand.json again
                                    (--pruefen: cont-init, --dienst: service)

Interactive start: when gh is not logged in, the menu begins with the
GitHub login (the student may cancel; then she is asked again next time).
After a GitHub login clawbook offers to take name and noreply address of
the GitHub account as git identity, and it offers once to renew an outdated
wsm configuration (the wsm wrapper does the same before wsm starts).
/etc/profile.d/zz-clawbook-menu.sh opens the menu on interactive SSH
logins; /usr/local/bin/wsm asks for the GitHub login before the first run
of the WorkspaceManager ("clawbook github login --vor-wsm").

Only the Python standard library is used. User-facing output is German.
The script works for the user "student" and for root (docker exec / wslc
exec run as root): files in the home directory always belong to "student".
"""

